meta {
  name: 9g. Verify Open Access (no token → 200)
  type: http
  seq: 28
  tags: [
    requires-nifi
  ]
}

get {
  url: {{apisixApiUrl}}/v1/datasets/{{sagaDataSetId}}/{{sagaSlug}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

script:pre-request {
  // 9f persisted openDataAccess=true. The route always carries OIDC + OPA (no bypass); OPA now
  // reads the dataset's open-data flag and allows the anonymous read (ABAC). Poll the data-plane
  // WITHOUT a token until it returns 200, max ~50s (25 attempts × 2s) to absorb any propagation
  // (DB commit + OPA fetch). While the dataset is still protected the gateway answers 401.
  // Bruno's QuickJS axios does not honour a validateStatus function, so it throws on non-2xx;
  // catch the 401 (still-protected) state instead of letting it abort the loop.
  const axios = require('axios');
  // Per-NamedApi route model (#1368): the public data-plane path is per slug.
  const slug = bru.getVar('sagaSlug') || 'things';
  const url = `${bru.getEnvVar('apisixApiUrl')}/v1/datasets/${bru.getVar('sagaDataSetId')}/${slug}`;
  for (let i = 0; i < 25; i++) {
    let status = 0;
    try { status = (await axios.get(url)).status; }
    catch (e) { status = e.response ? e.response.status : 0; }
    if (status === 200) break;
    await new Promise(res => setTimeout(res, 2000));
  }
}

tests {
  test("Open dataset is reachable through the gateway WITHOUT a token (200)", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("Response is valid JSON from FROST", function() {
    expect(res.body).to.be.an('object');
  });
}

docs {
  **Saga step 9g of 18** — Verify the open data-access workflow end-to-end (issue #1368, journeys J1/J3).

  After 9f flipped `openDataAccess` to true, an **unauthenticated** GET to `api.<host>/v1/datasets/{id}/{slug}` returns 200 — decided by **OPA** (ABAC on the dataset's open-data flag), not by a gateway bypass. The route keeps OIDC + OPA; OIDC passes the anonymous request through (`unauth_action: pass`) and OPA grants the open-data read. This is the counterpart to the protected path (9c → 401): together they cover both `openDataAccess` workflows (false **and** true).

  **Precondition:** 9f accepted; pre-request polled the data-plane until 200 (open-data flag visible to OPA).

  **Expected Response:** 200 OK, JSON body — no bearer token sent.
}
